vernor Maura Healey seeks a second term against Republican Mike Minogue, with independent Andrea James also on the ballot. Polling throughout 2026 has shown Healey with a wide lead, including a mid-October Suffolk University survey putting her ahead 59-36 and an October UMass Amherst poll at 56-31. Her advantage has stayed in the high teens to mid-20s across more than a year of surveys from several pollsters.\n\nThe state's strong Democratic lean, Healey's incumbency, and consistent Solid D ratings from every major forecaster all point the same direction. Prediction markets put her chances near 96 percent. Minogue has emphasized affordability and tried to present himself as a moderate, but coverage suggests limited traction, and national conditions weigh on Republicans in Massachusetts. The race is rated Safe D, with the main question being the size of Healey's winning margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin"